  "budget": {
    "$doc": "D23/D42 — the build gate. Measured against world.report.stats out of a real headless load, never by eye. See BUILD.md for why the heap row differs from the spec's number.",
    "$collidableTriangles": [
      "specs/0025 — THE SOURCE OF TRUTH IS bench/public/js/play/collision.js, and",
      "this number is a copy of it. collision.js:196 reads",
      "`const triBudget = opts.triBudget || 1200000;` — 0018 raised it from 900000",
      "because the soup already stood at 895,689 against a ceiling that fails",
      "CLOSED (over the cap, a group is silently truncated rather than reported),",
      "and 0018 was about to declare five more prop groups: sign-posts,",
      "people-props, poulsen-props, kt-summit-props and deck-benches, +10,846",
      "triangles between them. It never moved this copy, so from 0018 onward every",
      "HEAD build measured 906,522 against a 900,000 cap it could not meet —",
      "renders/gate-rca/RCA.md §3.",
      "",
      "Measured on the 0025 build, after the arena-furniture split took 1,078",
      "triangles back out: 905,444 (class histogram [snow 774,618, rock 16,781,",
      "building 55,393, tower 49,504, person 8,728, bench 420]). Siberia measures",
      "far less and carries the same number for the same reason worlds/siberia.json",
      "carries the rest of world #1's caps: they are deliberately unrelaxed.",
      "",
      "Two ceilings that disagree is the defect this fixes; one number in two",
      "places is the cost of the gate reading the manifest and the player reading",
      "its own module. If you want the gate noisy about growth, tighten THIS one",
      "(a 950,000 would still clear today's harvest by 44,556) and leave",
      "collision.js alone — a gate cap below the harvester's cap only reports, but",
      "a harvester cap below the truth silently drops geometry."
    ],
